From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwcn: free the firmware buffer, not the advanced data pointer

marlin_request_firmware() reads the firmware into a vmalloc() buffer and
points both mfirmware->data and mfirmware->priv at it.
marlin_firmware_parse_image() then advances data past the WCNM pack
header to the image selected for the chip (and the function-mask path
advances it by 8), but priv keeps the original address.

marlin_release_firmware() frees mfirmware->data. With a WCNM pack such
as wcnmodem-38222.bin this is not the address vmalloc() returned, so
vfree() warns ("Trying to vfree() nonexistent vm area") and the buffer
leaks on every power-on:

  WARNING: mm/vmalloc.c:3342 at remove_vm_area+0x60/0x6c
  WARNING: mm/vmalloc.c:3477 at vfree+0x260/0x284

The reload path in marlin_firmware_parse_image() already frees priv.
Do the same here.

Tested on a ZTE W132D (UWE5623, Marlin3E AB) with wcnmodem-38222.bin.

Signed-off-by: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c
@@ -1291,7 +1291,12 @@
 		if (mfirmware->is_from_fs)
 			release_firmware(mfirmware->priv);
 		else
-			vfree(mfirmware->data);
+			/*
+			 * data may have been advanced past the WCNM pack header
+			 * (marlin_firmware_parse_image) or the 8-byte function
+			 * mask; priv still holds what vmalloc() returned.
+			 */
+			vfree(mfirmware->priv);
 		kfree(mfirmware);
 	}
 }
